<div class="work"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="{{ 'hypr-ing-scoop.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="A scoop of creatine powder"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 · Perform</p><h3>Creatine monohydrate</h3><p>Creatine tops up the fast fuel your muscles use for sprints, jumps and lifts. Sports nutrition experts (ISSN) call monohydrate the most effective supplement for high-intensity training.*</p><span class="ref mono">[1] Kreider et al., J Int Soc Sports Nutr, 2017</span></div></div>
<div class="work"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="{{ 'hypr-ing-swirl.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Collagen dissolving in water"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 · Support</p><h3>Collagen peptides</h3><p>Collagen gives you glycine and proline, the building blocks of tendons and ligaments. Research here is newer than for creatine, so we keep the claim simple.*</p><span class="ref mono">[4] Shaw et al., Am J Clin Nutr, 2017</span></div></div>
